{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["אל נא תהי כמת — that is, for your honor and on your account, do not you yourself be like a dead man. And how? אשר נולד בצאתו — one who is born from his innards — מרחם אמו — of his brother who is alive — הרי נאכל חצי בשרו — half the flesh of the living. That is: since Miriam was born from the womb of the mother of Moshe." "אל נא תהי — do not you be like a dead man, as in: ״אל תהי בתקעי כף״, ״אל תהי עד חנם״, ״אל תהי בסובאי יין״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The comment unpacks the verse's comparison phrase by inserting explanatory glosses between the words; the final sentence appears to trail off, explaining that Miriam shares the same mother as Moshe."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:06.934163728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}